@ 29.1.1.1.15 - Proto-Athabaskan to Upper Koyukon
# citation: Whimemsz, from Krauss, Michael and Victor Golla (1981), “Northern Athapaskan Languages”. Handbook of North American Indians, Vol. 6 (Subarctic), 67 – 85 Stem-final/suffixal consonant clusters lost in Minchumina-Bearpaw Upper Koyukon
	{ e, a, ɑ, ʊ } > { a, o, ŏ, ŭ }
	{ TS, {TŠ,TŠʷ} } > { TŁ, TS }
	[+ cons, - fr, + bk, + hi, - lo] > TŠ
	C’ > C / _$
	Vˀ > V:[+low tone]
	V:[+low tone] > V:[-tone]
	w > m / _Vn (sporadic)
	w > b